\f0\fs48 \cf9 4.1 Grid - Proposed solutions\

\fs40 \cf10 Action planned\
developments urgently\

\fs20 NIE Network\'92s proposed RP7 business plan (2025-\
2031) details the required level of grid investment\
needed to meet NI\'92s climate change commitments.\
While the ambition is welcomed by industry, the\
proposal highlights the magnitude of what is\
needed, with a c\'a32.6bn investment required over\
the period and 1,000 new jobs created.\
The network needs the delivery of a large-scale\
project to significantly upgrade and reinforce the\
network.\
Providing the Utility Regulator with the vires to\
consider environmental and climate priorities\
would further support necessary grid\
developments.\

\fs40 Innovate to address\
skills shortage\

\fs20 Another key challenge around grid development is\
a potential skills shortage, particularly in relation\
to electrical engineering.\
This skills shortage is seen as an Achilles\'92 heel to\
achieving climate change targets given the\
reliance on grid infrastructure development.\
Some possibilities to address this are:\
1) Apprentices and graduates.\
2) Use of contractors.\
3) Development of turnkey solutions for standard\
projects which are not as labour/skills intensive.\

\fs16 \cf8 Source: NIE Newtork\'92s 2030 network vision as detailed in the RP7 business plan summary.\

